speechtext:
Perhaps that question could
best be answered by giving the different items in the vote and showing where there are increases and decreases. In travelling expenses of head office staff, $8,000 was expended in
1935-	36; the estimate for 1936-37 is $9,000, or an increase of $1,000. Outside administration, salaries and expenses: 1935-36, $222,790.48;
1936-	37, $225,407, an increase of $2,616.52. Rental of offices and railway spur: $1,393 in
1935-	36 and $1,535 for 1936-37, an increase of $142. Shipping point and export inspection, salaries and expenses: 1935-36, $187.322.50;
1936-	37, $174,090, a decrease of $13,232.50.
Operation of onion warehouses:	1935-36,
SI,500; 1936-37, $200, a decrease of $1,300. car precooling: $1,500 in 1935-36; $1,000 for 1936-37, a decrease of $500. There is an item covering exhibitions which has been taken over by the publicity and extension branch. The amount expended in 1935-36 was $3,500, so there is a decrease of that amount in this branch, but there is not a decrease in the total expenditures. Extending markets, test shipments: 1935-36, $2,000; 1936-37, $2,000, no increase or decrease. The amounts are the same for equipment and repairs of onion warehouses, $800 for each year. The amount for technical instruments, transportation and warehouses is the same for each year, $500. Publications and bulletins: $3,500 for each year. Crop and market reports, telegrams, et cetera: $12,000 for each
year. Office supplies, stationery, forms, equipment, et cetera: 1935-36, $15,800; 1936-37, $16,800, an increase of $1,000. Apple maggot survey, eastern provinces:	1935-36, $8,000;
1936-37, $6,000, a decrease of $2,000. The amount for legal services is the same for each year, $1,500. Repairs to departmental cars: $1,000 for each year. Grant to horticultural council: 1935-36, $4,500; estimated for this year, $4,750, an increase of $250.
